Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: bfd/coffgen.c
Line: 2596
Function: coff_find_nearest_line_with_names
Bug type: out-of-bounds-read
CWE: CWE-125
Explanation: After positioning s within the raw symbol table, the code only checks that s is within bounds, then if s->u.syment.n_numaux is nonzero it reads (s+1)->u.auxent. There is no check that s+1 is still within the array, so a crafted file can place s at the last entry while claiming n_numaux != 0, causing an out-of-bounds read of the aux entry.

